          {
            "citations": null,
            "text": "<action>\ncurl -X POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.list \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"token=<TOKEN>&types=public_channel,private_channel&limit=100\"\n</action>\n\nNow let me search for the mentorship-hub channel in the results and get its details, then I'll fetch its members:\n\n<action>\ncurl -X POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.list \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"token=<TOKEN>&types=public_channel,private_channel\" | grep -i \"mentorship-hub\"\n</action>\n\nLet me get the channel info more directly:\n\n<action>\ncurl -X POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.list \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"token=<TOKEN>&types=public_channel,private_channel&limit=200\"\n</action>\n\nLet me check the full response and extract the channel ID properly:\n\n<action>\ncurl -s -X POST https://slack.com/api/conversations.list \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"token=<TOKEN>&types=public_channel,private_channel&limit=200\" | python3 -m json.tool\n</action>\n\nLet me try a simpler approach - search for messages from the #mentorship-hub channel and add a reaction:\n\n<action>\ncurl -s -X POST https://slack.com/api/search.messages \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"token=<TOKEN>&query=in%3Amentorship-hub&count=10\"\n</action>",
